Why a second licence
--------------------
The code is MIT so it can be freely reused, patched and embedded. The skin and
the copy exist only because this is a fan work about a specific game, and the
people who made that game own its identity. Keeping the two licences apart means
a developer can take the code without ever taking a claim on the artwork, and
nobody can strip the non-commercial guard off the parts that would embarrass the
project if they were sold.

